  [1m3. Consequence you should know about[0m

  Once [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is a module, opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m by double-clicking stops working — browsers block module loads over
  [38;5;153mfile://[39m. You'll need [38;5;153mpython3 -m http.server 8000[39m or similar. That's inherent to the ESM choice, not something I can
  code around.

  Two open decisions below, then I'll write the spec.

  [1mThe fork on fallback:[0m an unrecognized hostname has to resolve to [3msomething[0m. Defaulting to [38;5;153mprod[39m means a forgotten
  domain still works in production but an unknown dev box silently talks to the live API. Defaulting to [38;5;153mdev[39m means an
  unknown host can never hit production, but a mis-typed prod domain breaks the live site loudly. Throwing means neither
  happens silently, but any hostname gap is a blank page. I recommend [1mdev[0m — the worst case is a broken staging page,
  not real users' credentials going somewhere unintended, and the wrongness is visible immediately.

